From e9397456f6fffe1b765d38b22ac9033c0ab18d84 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RDoom <171243930+aeon1911@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 10:03:19 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 16/66] Vulkan on Switch: step-by-step session log,
 unified-memory buffers, safe shader polling.

- Instance, VI surface, device, swapchain and presented-frame count are written
  to the session report; a Vulkan failure is a clear fatal error that tells the
  user to pick OpenGL/OpenGL ES explicitly (no silent fallback).
- Static/stream buffers are written in place on the Tegra X1's unified memory
  instead of staging + vkCmdCopyBuffer (which NVK runs as a compute shader).
- Timestamp query pool is created on the first 'stat gpu' only.
- VkShaderManager/FShaderManager::CompileNextShader return 'done' when polled
  again after finishing (the Switch start-up precompile loop did that and read
  defaultshaders[-1]).
- Mesa 26 glthread is chosen with MESA_SWITCH_GLTHREAD; the Mesa 20.1
  structure-offset patching is no longer used.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
